2), with the changed set equal to `{new-caller}`, and the incident replay (AC-9.3). The six copies are held equal by the equivalence test (AC-9.4), so one copy cannot carry a broader exception. DO-7 says where the rule is applied. |"},{"line_number":957,"content":"  and the direct-call replay of T5/T6 in AC-9.3 (D), and AC-9.4 for the six copies (A). Spec v1.7"},{"line_number":976,"content":"    residual that follows. Place the AC-9.4 equivalence test, which the plan has named, give each"},{"line_number":994,"content":"- v1.3: Final corrective revision after the plan audit round cap: cycle-2 build findings only, and spec v1.5 at e8def13f (2026-10-16). A: stage 6 and DO-7 bind the six copies of the FR-9 carve-out to one authority (AC-9.4). The plan names the equivalence test and carries a one-copy-per-row mutation control. B: stage 6 rewrites the SKILL.md teammate-audit bullet to separate audit-leg selection from resolved authorship (resolved = claude), and pins the replacement condition (baseline 0/0 at 9c3b799d); Success Criteria lists it. C: the FR-9 census adds surface 5, the h_mad_assemble_tdd.py assemble() wiring header, and its pin in test_h_mad_assemble_tdd.py. The census states the split-across-a-line-break class and its joined-literal sweep (7 files at 9c3b799d). D: the incident replay names the three pin files and commits, and replays T5/T6 in direct-call form, recording the scaffolded RED. E: the doc-pin census adds the missed pins from test_h_mad_tdd_gate_docs.py and test_grok_fallback_do [... truncated (1031 chars total)]"}]}]},"locations":[]}
