{"type":"tool_call_update","toolCallId":"call-51c4053e-280a-4ece-8574-c484f99540ad-20","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"210→| `TDD-IMPLEMENTER: <codex\\|agy> chosen=<peer> switch=<peer>-><peer> reason=<env\\|status\\|cli-absent>` | automatic peer switch | stage the resolved peer; print the line on the dispatch |\n| `TDD-IMPLEMENTER: <grok\\|claude> chosen=<peer> switch=peers-out reason=<chosen peer's reason>` | both peers out | today's fallback path, unchanged |\n| `TDD-IMPLEMENTER: invalid field=<implementer\\|fallback_agent> value=<pct-encoded>` | record holds an invalid value | halt `step5:implementer_invalid`; fix the record; never dispatch |\n| `TDD-IMPLEMENTER: no-record feature=<pct-encoded>` | no such feature in the state file | halt `step5:implementer_unresolved`; the feature name or root is wrong |\n| `TDD-IMPLEMENTER: unreadable file=<pct-encoded> error=<name>` | state file cannot be read | halt `step5:implementer_unresolved`, same as the gate's unreadable state |\n\n**Halts (v1.10, adopted from impl-plan v1.1 Task 16).** The verb's caller has exactly three halts,\none per failure class of the token above: `step5:implementer_invalid` (an `invalid` token: the\nrecord is wrong and a human fixes it), `step5:implementer_unresolved` (a `no-record` or\n`unreadable` token: the verb could not reach a record), and `step5:implementer_switch_unrecorded`\n220→(any token with ` record=failed`, below). The three tokens that name a peer (`switch=none`, a peer switch,\n`peers-out`) halt nothing. Residual: `failure-recovery.md` gains no row for any of the three\nhalts in this feature (impl-plan v1.1 adds none); a recovery row for them is owed to a later\nfeature, not settled here.\n\nWith `--record`, any `switch` other than `none` writes `implementer_switch` to the record through\n`h_mad_state_write.py`'s write path, so the claim and session rules apply. The write is skipped\nwhen the stored value already has the same `from`, `to` and `reason`, which keeps re-staging\nidempotent. A failed write prints the token with ` record=failed` appended. The caller halts\n`step5:implementer_switch_unrecorded`, because a switch that is not in state is exactly the\n230→silent switch the operator decision forbids.\n\n`h_mad_assemble_tdd.py` remains state-independent (`test_state_fallback_agent_is_not_read` stays\ngreen). The orchestrator runs the verb and passes the result as `--agent`.\n\n### FR-3 — Claude-side authorship gate\n\n`h-mad-tdd-gate.sh` folds every `step5` record on the chain, as it does today. Precedence is\nfirst match wins:\n"}}],"rawOutput":{"type":"ReadFile","FileContent":{"content":"210→| `TDD-IMPLEMENTER: <codex\\|agy> chosen=<peer> switch=<peer>-><peer> reason=<env\\|status\\|cli-absent>` | automatic peer switch | stage the resolved peer; print the line on the dispatch |\n| `TDD-IMPLEMENTER: <grok\\|claude> chosen=<peer> switch=peers-out reason=<chosen peer's reason>` | both peers out | today's fallback path, unchanged |\n| `TDD-IMPLEMENTER: invalid field=<implementer\\|fallback_agent> value=<pct-encoded>` | record holds an invalid value | halt `step5:implementer_invalid`; fix the record; never dispatch |\n| `TDD-IMPLEMENTER: no-record feature=<pct-encoded>` | no such feature in the state file | halt `step5:implementer_unresolved`; the feature name or root is wrong |\n| `TDD-IMPLEMENTER: unreadable file=<pct-encoded> error=<name>` | state file cannot be read | halt `step5:implementer_unresolved`, same as the gate's unreadable state |\n\n**Halts (v1.10, adopted from impl-plan v1.1 Task 16).** The verb's caller has exactly three halts,\none per failure class of the token above: `step5:implementer_invalid` (an `invalid` token: the\nrecord is wrong and a human fixes it), `step5:implementer_unresolved` (a `no-record` or\n`unreadable` token: the verb could not reach a record), and `step5:implementer_switch_unrecorded`\n220→(any token with ` record=failed`, below). The three tokens that name a peer (`switch=none`, a peer switch,\n`peers-out`) halt nothing. Residual: `failure-recovery.md` gains no row for any of the three\nhalts in this feature (impl-plan v1.1 adds none); a recovery row for them is owed to a later\nfeature, not settled here.\n\nWith `--record`, any `switch` other than `none` writes `implementer_switch` to the record through\n`h_mad_state_write.py`'s write path, so the claim and session rules apply. The write is skipped\nwhen the stored value already has the same `from`, `to` and `reason`, which keeps re-staging\nidempotent. A failed write prints the token with ` record=failed` appended. The caller halts\n`step5:implementer_switch_unrecorded`, because a switch that is not in state is exactly the\n230→silent switch the operator decision forbids.\n\n`h_mad_assemble_tdd.py` remains state-independent (`test_state_fallback_agent_is_not_read` stays\ngreen). The orchestrator runs the verb and passes the result as `--agent`.\n\n### FR-3 — Claude-side authorship gate\n\n`h-mad-tdd-gate.sh` folds every `step5` record on the chain, as it does today. Precedence is\nfirst match wins:\n","content_concise":"210→| `TDD-IMPLEMENTER: <codex\\|agy> chosen=<peer> switch=<peer>-><peer> reason=<env\\|status\\|cli-absent>` | automatic peer switch | stage the resolved peer; print the line on the dispatch |\n| `TDD-IMPLEMENTER: <grok\\|claude> chosen=<peer> switch=peers-out reason=<chosen peer's reason>` | both peers out | today's fallback path, unchanged |\n| `TDD-IMPLEMENTER: invalid field=<implementer\\|fallback_agent> value=<pct-encoded>` | record holds an invalid value | halt `step5:implementer_invalid`; fix the record; never dispatch |\n| `TDD-IMPLEMENTER: no-record feature=<pct-encoded>` | no such feature in the state file | halt `step5:implementer_unresolved`; the feature name or root is wrong |\n| `TDD-IMPLEMENTER: unreadable file=<pct-encoded> error=<name>` | state file cannot be read | halt `step5:implementer_unresolved`, same as the gate's unreadable state |\n\n**Halts (v1.10, adopted from impl-plan v1.1 Task 16).** The verb's caller has exactly three halts,\none per failure class of the token above: `step5:implementer_invalid` (an `invalid` token: the\nrecord is wrong and a human fixes it), `step5:implementer_unresolved` (a `no-record` or\n`unreadable` token: the verb could not reach a record), and `step5:implementer_switch_unrecorded`\n220→(any token with ` record=failed`, below). The three tokens that name a peer (`switch=none`, a peer switch,\n`peers-out`) halt nothing. Residual: `failure-recovery.md` gains no row for any of the three\nhalts in this feature (impl-plan v1.1 adds none); a recovery row for them is owed to a later\nfeature, not settled here.\n\nWith `--record`, any `switch` other than `none` writes `implementer_switch` to the record through\n`h_mad_state_write.py`'s write path, so the claim and session rules apply. The write is skipped\nwhen the stored value already has the same `from`, `to` and `reason`, which keeps re-staging\nidempotent. A failed write prints the token with ` record=failed` appended. The caller halts\n`step5:implementer_switch_unrecorded`, because a switch that is not in state is exactly the\n230→silent switch the operator decision forbids.\n\n`h_mad_assemble_tdd.py` remains state-independent (`test_state_fallback_agent_is_not_read` stays\ngreen). The orchestrator runs the verb and passes the result as `--agent`.\n\n### FR-3 — Claude-side authorship gate\n\n`h-mad-tdd-gate.sh` folds every `step5` record on the chain, as it does today. Precedence is\nfirst match wins:\n","absolute_path":"/Users/kimhawk/.local/state/h-mad/grok-audit-surface/run-ab2c85dc2e25-20261024T132452Z/roots/gas-root-d7-s2v1-jev07wj7/docs/01-plan/features/agy-coder-fallback.spec.md","offset":210,"limit":30,"raw_output":"| `TDD-IMPLEMENTER: <codex\\|agy> chosen=<peer> switch=<peer>-><peer> reason=<env\\|status\\|cli-absent>` | automatic peer switch | stage the resolved peer; print the line on the d