t_is_not_read` stays\ngreen). The orchestrator runs the verb and passes the result as `--agent`.\n\n### FR-3 — Claude-side authorship gate\n\n`h-mad-tdd-gate.sh` folds every `step5` record on the chain, as it does today. Precedence is\nfirst match wins:\n\n","total_lines":1251}},"locations":[]}
{"type":"tool_call_update","toolCallId":"call-51c4053e-280a-4ece-8574-c484f99540ad-25","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"1185→  class-(b) target that names an existing directory is refused with `kind=judge-error` when the\n  scan reads `active` or `unknown`, and allowed when it reads `inactive` (FR-4 deliberate\n  difference 6). Reason: impl-plan v1.1 Task 6 showed that `canonicalise` returns no name and\n  no `unresolvable` flag for `.`, `src/`, `src` and the root, so the class-(b) sequence would\n  otherwise allow a directory target under `active`. Residual: a trailing-`/` path that names no\n1190→  existing directory is not covered and is judged as a file name.\n\n## Open questions for the operator\n\nNone — OQ-1/OQ-2 settled 2026-10-16; the design's OQ-A/OQ-B settled 2026-10-16 (D-12, D-13);\nthe design's OD-E2 settled 2026-10-16 (D-15); the impl-plan's OD-2 settled 2026-10-16 (D-16).\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- Per-task implementer selection. It can come later on the same field.\n1200→- Refusing a peer's production write in that peer's own gate when the other peer is the resolved\n  implementer, for example a Codex verifier dispatch writing production code under\n  `implementer=agy`. Residual: the test-first judge still applies, and the per-dispatch\n  `git status --short` diff (agy-runtime.md §\"Author and reviewer roles\") is what shows it.\n- A write-time gate for grok, and authorship rules for agy as the orchestrating host.\n- Routing audit legs by `agy_status`.\n\n## Owed by other documents\n\nNone of these are edited by this spec.\n1210→- `h-mad/references/agy-runtime.md` says there is no `SessionStart` on two surfaces:\n  - §\"Hooks\" (\"There is **no `SessionStart`**\");\n  - the §\"Construct mapping\" table's `hook-event` row (\"there is no `SessionStart`\").\n\n  agy's current hooks.md lists `SessionStart` as a supported event. Both surfaces need a re-check\n  against the installed agy (`agy --version` prints 1.4.0 at `200ffd52`), they are corrected\n  together, and the correction stamps the version it was checked against.\n  (`grep -n 'SessionStart' h-mad/references/agy-runtime.md` at `200ffd52`: 2 matching lines, one\n  under each heading.) Residual: this is a content predicate, so a third restatement added later\n  is found only by re-running the grep.\n1220→- **Design (v1.8 items).** FR-4: enumerate the closed kind list and give every deny path a member\n  (E6); its claim that `unknown` \"denies `kind=judge-error`, as the Codex gate does for a shell\n  command\" is false at `cff71b49` — the Codex gate's `unknown` shell deny carries no `kind=`\n  token. FR-7: name where the complete author set is kept (E2) and correct \"the GREEN dispatch the\n  orchestrator accepted at 5d\" to 5e (E4).\n- **Design (v1.9, D-15).** FR-1: add `implementation_authors` with FR-1's entry schema to the\n  schema JSON and a `state-schema.md` row. FR-7: retire \"the complete set is kept in the\n  procedure\" and OD-E2 in favour of reading the set from `implementation_authors`; the\n  `--append` mechanism (DO-3) must accept this key with the same guarantees, and the \"When the\n  dispatch list is lost\" rule becomes FR-7's three closed unrecoverable cases.\n1230→- **Design (spec v1.10).** FR-4: record D-16 as a directory check before the target is judged,\n  and add it to §\"Deliberate differences\" as item 6; FR-4 `--self-check`: a verdict `FAIL` exits\n  0 (replacing \"a nonzero exit\"), and the Codex gate's `FAIL shell-policy` is corrected in impl-plan\n  Task 4; FR-2: adopt the halts `step5:implementer_invalid` and `step5:implementer_unresolved`.\n- **Impl-plan.** AC-7.3's surface (FR-7 §\"Attribution\" must have code to drive, or the AC is an\n  OPEN-DECISION), now including the pre-field fixture; AC-1.3's fixtures; AC-4.1's `unknown`\n  fixtures and AC-4.2's per-deny-path kind fixtures.\n- **Plan.** If the plan carries FR-1's field list or AC-7.3's fixtures, it gains\n  `implementation_a