udit-leg selection from resolved authorship (resolved = claude), and pins the replacement condition (baseline 0/0 at 9c3b799d); Success Criteria lists it. C: the FR-9 census adds surface 5, the h_mad_assemble_tdd.py assemble() wiring header, and its pin in test_h_mad_assemble_tdd.py. The census states the split-across-a-line-break class and its joined-literal sweep (7 files at 9c3b799d). D: the incident replay names the three pin files and commits, and replays T5/T6 in direct-call form, recording the scaffolded RED. E: the doc-pin census adds the missed pins from test_h_mad_tdd_gate_docs.py and test_grok_fallback_do [... truncated (1031 chars total)]"},{"line_number":995,"content":"- v1.4: Answers the advisory delta review of v1.3 (2026-10-16), no new scope. Must-fix 1 and Should-fix 1: stage 6 and DO-7 no longer read the assembler copy from the assembled wiring prompt; each of the six copies is read from its own source location (each template copy located individually, the .py copy from its joined str constant), the locators are a DO-7 obligation that must make a single-copy mutation fail the test, and each mutation row's find carries context unique in its file because the harness refuses a non-unique anchor. Should-fix 2: canonical carve-out sentence becomes the canonical carve-out block (all three sentences of spec FR-9's block) at stage 6, DO-7 and the Design owed line. Should-fix 3: the FR-9 census states that the joined-literal reading cannot see .py comments or parse failures, the AC-9.1 re-run takes the union with the line grep, re-measured at 5f72c2f3 (union 7 files, comment hits 0, parse failures 0), and the spec item is listed as owed. Should-fix 4: DO [... truncated (1031 chars total)]"}]}]},"locations":[]}
